Title: 200 AMSTERDAM: THE VERTICAL CITY
Credit: Written for the Screen by
Author: Danny Bouldiez
Source: Adapted from the Novel "200 AMSTERDAM"
Episode: PART 00A: THE KINETIC THREAD (FOREWORD & PREFACE)

====

EXT. SPACE - ORBITAL VIEW OF EARTH - NIGHT

A silent, cosmic void. Earth glows below—a sapphire sphere crisscrossed by delicate webs of gold city lights. 

A DEEP, PULSING BASS HUM begins. Low. Vibrational. 18 Hz.

SUPER: "I believe everything in this universe is bound by an unbroken kinetic thread."

CAMERA DRIFTS closer to the blue swirl of the Antarctic ice shelf.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
A single event is never just a single event—it is the first domino in a chain reaction of forces we rarely see coming.

EXT. WEST ANTARCTIC ICE SHEET - DAY

A colossal shelf of glacial ice—miles long, centuries old—GROANS. 

A fracture line, thin as a hair, ZIPS across the white crust with the sound of a high-velocity rifle crack. 

A billion-ton block of ice shears off and PLUMMETS into the black sea. 

NARRATOR (V.O.)
In human lives, the fracture can start with the loss of a job, which ripples into financial pressure, strains a relationship, takes a home away, and unravels a life. 

INT. MANHATTAN SUBWAY TUNNEL - CONTINUOUS

Water DROPS from a concrete ceiling arch. 

A puddle on the subway tracks ripples in perfect concentric circles. A rhythmic tremor shivers through the rails.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
On a planetary scale, the melting of ancient polar ice shifts billions of tons of mass, subtly altering the Earth's rotation, igniting telluric currents beneath our tectonic plates, and hurling ocean surges through concrete canyons.

EXT. UPPER WEST SIDE - 200 AMSTERDAM AVENUE - SUNSET

The 70-story glass needle of 200 Amsterdam gleams in the dying golden light of Manhattan. Impossibly sleek. Impossibly tall. 

NARRATOR (V.O.)
We live revolving around one another in a world that is revolving around us. The oceans are not separate from the bedrock; the bedrock is not separate from the atmosphere; and the air we breathe is not separate from the human heart.

SUPER: 
"I'm spinning round and round,
Fortune's a bitch with no solid ground.
One day you're down, next day you fly,
Then boom—who's to say? Just ask the sky."

NARRATOR (V.O.)
When the ground fractures and the systems we built fail to protect us, Love is not a luxury or a sentimental concept—it is the single most vital element in the continuity of our species. 

A sudden, violent JOLT shakes the camera. The glass tower shudders.

FADE TO BLACK.
